@carlescufi I can work but I need some help to understand my options inside a timer callback to change **ctx->trx_state** variable.
```
static void trx_isr_timeout(struct k_timer *timer_id)
{
	struct rf2xx_context *ctx = (struct rf2xx_context *)
				    k_timer_user_data_get(timer_id);

	k_mutex_lock(&ctx->phy_mutex, K_FOREVER);
	ctx->trx_state = RF2XX_TRX_PHY_STATE_IDLE;
	k_mutex_unlock(&ctx->phy_mutex);
}
```
This callback affects transceiver state machine and mistakes around that variable could lead to a deadlock.

Need refactor name from **trx_isr_timeout** to **trx_timeout_callback** too.
